# CI/CD Test Pipeline Essentials

## Test Tier System (fastest/most-critical → slowest/broadest)

| Tier | Scope | Trigger |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **0 Smoke** | Critical path (5–10) | Every commit |
| **1 Sanity** | Core features (20–50) | Every PR |
| **2 Selective** | Change-based | On merge |
| **3 Full** | Complete regression | Nightly / pre-release |

## Non-Negotiable Rules

- **Tag by tier** for selective execution via TestNG groups / suite XML (e.g. smoke, sanity, regression)
- **Parallelism**: prefer existing TestNG parallel suites (`testng-*-parallel.xml`) and CI job split over inventing new runners
- **Retries CI-only**: keep local runs fail-fast; use CI retry/quarantine policies deliberately
- **Deployment gates**: smoke must pass before broader regression stages (`needs:` in workflow)
- **Test data in CI**: environment variables for secrets (never hardcode); CI-specific data; seed before / truncate after
- **Artifacts on failure**: upload Allure results/reports and screenshots on failure

